# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability suppression list
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  (one per line, with a comment explaining why)
#
# Only suppress CVEs that are:
#   - Confirmed not exploitable in our threat model (with justification)
#   - Fixed in a version not yet available in our base image
#   - False positives confirmed by the upstream project
#
# NEVER suppress critical vulnerabilities without a documented justification.

# Example (uncomment and adapt as needed):
# CVE-2023-XXXXX  # Not exploitable: library used in test-only path, no network exposure
